---
heading:
  en: About the lab
  zhHant: 關於實驗室
---
The Novel Inorganic Materials Lab was founded in August 2025 by Prof. Yi-Teng Huang, within
the Graduate Institute of Photonics and Optoelectronics and the Department of Electrical
Engineering at National Taiwan University. We are based in R404 of EE Building II.

We are a young group, and that is deliberate: the problems we work on do not belong cleanly to
chemistry, physics or electrical engineering, and we would rather assemble people who are
willing to learn each other's methods than specialists who stay in their lane.

Our approach runs from synthesis through to devices. We make the material, measure what its
charge carriers do in the first picoseconds after absorbing a photon, and then build something
with it — a solar cell, a photodetector, an X-ray detector — to find out whether we understood
it correctly.
